WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.980
We have a winner!

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.440
An all-inclusive family hot springs trip for five!

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:11.360
You did it, Hakuya!

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.660
Wow! That's the grand prize!

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.470
Nice one, Hakuya-kun.

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:20.200
Here are your five tickets and a hot springs guide pamphlet.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.940
Congratulations!

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:22.680
Thanks.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:27.540
Gosh, you won, you know. Why not act a little happier?

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:30.420
Happier?

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.920
Oh, he looks pretty pleased.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.970
They said you can go to any of the hot springs in here.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:42.580
Hakuya won the drawing, so why don't we let him pick?

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.830
I don't really...

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.350
Ah! Here! I wanna go here!

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.980
UMA hot springs!

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.280
UMA hot springs?

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.180
That's a thing?

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:55.360
Arima Onsen

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.360
No, that's... not how you read that.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.140
Oh, then what about this one?

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.870
UMA Village?

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:06.500
I've seen this on TV before. It's famous for all the UMAs that appear there.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:11.150
They have a dinosaur like Nessie, tsuchinoko, giants lizards...

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:14.300
I dunno, it sounds a little fishy...

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:19.010
No, this is great! Let's go with this UMA Village! Absolutely!

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.670
Mashiro-chan, I thought you were afraid of things like UMAs and aliens?

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.890
But that's what makes them so great!

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:30.070
It's like, the draw of the strange and unknown!

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:32.830
Let's go with that then.

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:33.870
That easily?!

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.840
Yay!

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:45.160
Thanks for letting me come along even though it's a family trip.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:50.130
Mom was busy with work, anyway. It'd be a shame to let one ticket go to waste.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.470
I can't wait to see the UMA Village!

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:56.300
What kinds of UMAs are waiting for us?

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:01.990
I bet it's gonna be like that!

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:05.140
I doubt there will be dinosaurs in the baths...

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:08.110
Ah, I can't wait, either...

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:10.920
to get in the bath with Kobeni and Mashiro-tan.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.900
I think I'd be looking forward to it more if Benio weren't here.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:20.160
It's been tough lately, with Kobeni not taking baths with me anymore...

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:24.050
But this is a chance to bring back our culture of naked communication!

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:25.410
And of course...

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.910
Mashiro-tan...

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:32.040
Just imagining it is making me overheat!

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.860
Looks like Benio-san is excited too.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:38.550
I can pretty much imagine what she's thinking, though.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:44.060
<i>"Welcome to UMA Village"</i>

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.050
We're here!

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:47.430
Wow, it's really "UMA" everywhere.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:51.080
It's a total tourist destination.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:54.320
Whoa! A UMA already!

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.820
I'm pretty sure that's their mascot character...

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:04.080
Now that you mention it, I saw this in the pamphlet. It's the magic UMA, Magical Yuma-chan!

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.920
We may as well get a photo while she's here!

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:07.790
Okay.

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:11.790
Yay!

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.730
W-When did you-?!

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:17.050
Commemorative shot with Mashiro-tan: success!

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:21.130
I guess going on a trip gets everyone excited.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.550
It's like this all the time, though.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.810
What a beautiful place.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:32.810
It feels so mysterious.

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:36.810
Forget the scenery, what about the baths? Let's go already!

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.810
How did you get ready so fast?

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:44.570
Come now, let us join hands and dive headfirst into a dazzling bathtime world!

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:46.250
Come! Come! Come!

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:49.420
We have to change, so go on ahead of us.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:51.860
I believe there's an outdoor bath.

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:54.720
Okay. Don't be long now!

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:58.180
That's the wrong way to the bath, isn't it?

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:02.720
I'm not reckless enough to actually take a bath with Benio.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:09.210
This feels great.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:12.480
It really is different from your bath at home.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:17.880
The atmosphere is ideal! Perfect for a village of UMA!

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:22.510
I'm not sure how much of all that is really true...

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:29.540
Oh, about that. I did some research, and there's a lot of info that sounds pretty convincing.{I SAW IT ON THE INTERNET SO IT MUST BE TRUE}

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.270
Eh?!

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:35.120
It said a Nessie-like creature has been spotted in the lake we just saw.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:41.140
In the forest there are giant lizards, hairy monsters, and all kinds of mysterious life-forms!

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:42.630
N-No way...

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:46.120
Are you sure it's not just all marketing?

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:50.890
Hmm, I don't know, but it really does feel like you could run into something here!

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.910
Let's go looking later!

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:56.150
It'd be a shame to spend all of our time here in the bath!

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:59.650
I hope Nee-sama is okay.

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:04.650
Now come and join me, my adorable little sisters!

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:07.160
They're here!

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:15.910
I'll give them a fright. A surprise now and then is needed for communication, too.

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:19.710
WAAAAAAAAA

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.390
I'm not worried about Benio.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:31.130
If anything, the UMAs will be afraid of her.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.890
That may be true, but we did all come here together.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:36.390
I feel bad leaving Nee-sama out...

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.430
Is there really a dinosaur in here?!

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:46.100
That can't be possible!

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:51.660
Kobeni! Mashiro-tan! I finally found you!

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.650
I looked everywhere!

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:55.660
Where did you even come from?!

00:05:55.660 --> 00:06:01.290
The water here is connected with the outside bath. I went through there!

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.710
Nee-sama is a good swimmer.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:04.570
Really?

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:06.670
That's not the issue!

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:44.000
It sure is dark in the forest...

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.300
Don't worry. I'm prepared!

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.300
You look like you're on a television special.

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:53.430
She borrowed it from the inn, or something.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:56.000
Mashiro-chan, are you anxious?

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:00.560
Of course! I may finally have a face-to-face meeting with a UMA!

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.630
You don't seem very scared, Mayura.

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:06.070
Everyone is here, after all.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:12.000
You don't need all of that stuff, you'll be safe as long as you're by my side!

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.280
Having you with me just makes me scared in a completely different way!

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:18.300
W-What was that sound?

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:22.830
Could it be a giant lizard? Or maybe a Bigfoot?

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:25.840
Quiet. I'll investigate.

00:07:39.170 --> 00:07:41.660
Oh, it was a crow.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:42.420
Huh?

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:44.720
Where's Mashiro?

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:48.960
Hold on, Mashiro!

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:50.320
Mashiro!

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:52.200
I'll go.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.740
Nee-sama!

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:01.660
She's so fast!

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:04.960
At this rate, we'll get separated from everyone.

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:07.510
If that happens...

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:12.840
I'll be alone in the darkness... With Mashiro-tan...

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:20.470
Nooooooooo!!

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:32.320
Wait, Mashiro-tan!

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:34.180
Noooooooo!!

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:36.080
Well this is a pickle.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:39.830
We got separated from Mayura trying to find Nee-sama and Mashiro.

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:45.190
Mashiro has the map and compass... Where should we go?

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:46.130
It's okay.

00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:48.520
No matter what happens,

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:50.840
I'll protect you.

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:55.960
S-Seriously, how can you say those things so casually?!

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.560
W-What is it?

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:08.090
I'm beat...

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:10.640
Which way is it to the inn?

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:15.360
I don't know. Where even are we?

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:21.560
Oh, dear. You must have bumped it on something and broken it.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:25.810
It's your fault, Benio! You were the one chasing after me with that ridiculous expression!

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:27.960
I'll take responsibility, and marry you!

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:33.120
Even if we have to spend the rest of our lives in this forest, I'll support you!

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:34.460
No thank you!

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.840
What is that?

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:49.140
I don't know. That shadow... It's about the size of a person.

00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:50.090
It can't be...

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:52.190
Is it really a UMA?

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:55.150
It can't be a UMA, can it?

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.760
B-Be careful...

00:09:58.760 --> 00:09:59.700
Don't worry.

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:01.450
It's...

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.890
It might be...

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:09.040
Nee-sama! Mashiro!

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:14.540
I knew it'd be you two. Mashiro-tan, you can relax n-

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:16.970
Mashiro!

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:18.340
Oh dear, oh dear.

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:30.070
It's so pretty.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:35.250
Look, the inn is right over there.

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:38.870
That's amazing, Hakuya! Your sense of direction is perfect!

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:42.060
Kobeni-chan!

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:42.820
Mayura!

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:44.320
That's a relief.

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:46.580
I had no idea where you went!

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.880
Thank goodness I found you.

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:50.420
Sorry about that.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.310
You're awake?

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:59.480
L-L-L-Look at that! That!!

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:16.880
Could... That really be...?

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:20.280
No way... It must have been the shadow of a cloud or something.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:37.890
I really wonder what that thing last night was.

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:40.920
It was obviously a UMA! It has to be!

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:44.110
Ahh, I should have taken a picture!

00:11:44.110 --> 00:11:46.160
I wonder if it really was one.

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:47.810
What do you think, Hakuya?

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.550
If Mashiro says so...

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:52.520
It must have been a UMA.

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:58.280
Hmm? There's another UMA article over here.

00:11:58.280 --> 00:11:58.820
What?

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:04.090
"Last night, two mysterious shadows were seen flying around the perimeter of the lake."

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:10.730
"An eyewitness reported seeing two shadows jumping around at great speed while howling."

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:13.620
Isn't this talking about Mashiro and Nee-sama?

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:18.680
Why are we being treated like UMAs?! This is your fault too, Benio!

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:21.010
I'm sorry. I'll take responsibility and marry-

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:22.730
Give it a rest!

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:27.570
Don't you worry. I'll make this place into our personal paradise, Mashiro-tan!

00:12:27.570 --> 00:12:29.990
You stay behind and live with the UMAs!!
